 *//*
 * Definitions for IEEE 802.11 drivers.
 *//* for ieee80211_stats *//* min bg scan intvl (secs) *//* default bg scan intvl *//* min idle time (ms) *//* default idle time (ms) *//* max coverage class *//* max regclass id list *//* STA is in power saving mode *//* maximum saved packets *//* factor between xr Beacon interval and normal beacon interval *//* Default blacklist timeout (secs) *//* beacons allowed to miss before rescan *//*ms*//* Variants of the SM and MS macros that don't require a shift position macro *//* For Little-endian *//* Power constraing override *//* seconds *//* seconds *//* ms *//* ms *//* ms *//*
 * All Non-DFS channels are AVAILABLE by default
 * [AP] Any DFS channel is set to AVAILABLE:
 *	(i) only after CAC_DONE,
 *	(ii) and no radar was found
 * [STA] All DFS channels are NON_AVAILABLE by default.
 *
 *//* A DFS channel will stay in the NOT_AVAILABLE_RADAR_DETECTED state during the non-occupancy period *//* All DFS channels are marked as NOT_AVAILABLE_CAC_REQUIRED by default *//*
 * 802.11 control state is split into a common portion that maps
 * 1-1 to a physical device and one or more "Virtual AP's" (VAP)
 * that are bound to an ieee80211com instance and share a single
 * underlying device.  Each VAP has a corresponding OS device
 * entity through which traffic flows and that applications use
 * for issuing ioctls, etc.
 *//*
 * Data common to one or more virtual AP's.  State shared by
 * the underlying device and the net80211 layer is exposed here;
 * e.g. device-specific callbacks.
 *//* Sender address *//* Receiver address *//* Tx time - us *//* latest statistics data flag *//* unit: thousandth of air time *//* unit: minute *//* unit: minute *//* 1 - channel switching can be triggered; 0 - don't change channel *//* 1 - scs stats on; 0 - scs stats off *//* DFS-to-Non-DFS channel switch margin *//* index into the channel array *//* pmbl err range mapped to percent of cca intf *//* short preamble weight factor *//* long preamble weight factor *//* 1s based *//* 1s based *//* 0:normal, 1:less sensitive, 2:more sensitive *//* use qosnull frame to control the traffic *//* milliseconds, the time on off channel
								within one off-channel action, using qosnull
								with large NAV to protect the traffic *//* milliseconds, the time on off channel
							within 1 beacon interval *//* seconds, the total time for one channel *//* seconds, the total time on off channel
							for one channel *//* milliseconds, the time on weather channel
							within 1 beacon interval *//* seconds, the total time for weather channel *//* seconds, the total time on off channel
							for weather channel *//* percent, the threshold of FAT used to decide
							to run off-channel CAC *//* percent, the threshold of traffic used to
							decide to run ocac *//* percent, the threshold of consecutive FAT decrease,
							used to monitor the traffic variation *//* percent, the threshold of cca interference to
							decide to jump to off channel *//* milliseconds, the offset after sending
							beacon to halt tx in MuC *//* milliseconds, the offset after halt tx to
							switch to off channel in MuC*//* the ocac_timer interval *//* TUs, the beacon interval for OCAC *//* report mode, don't switch channel *//* ieee channel number, "0" means auto *//* the ocac_timer expire when starting ocac *//* the radar mode indicated by region *//* seconds, the accumulated off-channel
									CAC time for one channel*//* milliseconds, the accumulated time on
									off channel for one channel*//* current off channel for CAC *//* percent *//*
 * Channel occupancy record
 *//* time in seconds when channel was selected *//* channel for which time is recorded *//* previous channel *//* time spent on a channel in seconds *//* number of times channel was used *//* 8 mbps *//* 4 mbps *//* 5 seconds *//* STA BMPS timer for TX/RX *//* tput measurement *//* # of TX bytes in previous measurement *//* # of RX bytes in previous measurement *//* TX & RX overall throughput in kbps *//*
 * Operating class table for regulatory region to operating class conversion.
 *//*
 * Logical SSID group used for defining association limits per group of VAPs.
 *//* off channel suspend/resume expiration timer *//* off channel suspending counter *//* off channel suspending timeout, in jiffies *//* MATS FIX The member ic_dev is not used in QDRV and should be removed *//* associated device *//* state update lock *//* vap state machine lock *//* list of vap instances *//* XXX wrong for multi-mode *//* Phy Mode *//* Radar mode *//* operation mode *//* interface media config *//* mgmt/inactivity timer *//* state flags *//* extension of state flags *//* Quantenna specific flags *//* capabilities *//* VHT MCS capability *//* Current HT Max spatial streams *//* Current VHT Max spatial streams *//* Current 2.4G VHT Max spatial streams*//* Atheros adv. capabilities *//* vap's needing promisc mode *//* vap's needing all multicast*//* vap's been opened *//* set of mode capabilities *//* current mode *//* beacon interval *//* beacon interval for backup *//* PM hold over duration *//* beacon miss threshold (ms) *//* global tx power limit *//* sampling rate in seconds *//* tx power limit to change to (in 0.5 dBm) *//* max triggers that could arrive *//* coverage class *//* Num of scans after which gain settings toggle *//* RTS-CTS protection support *//* 11n Capabilities *//* HT capabilities *//* LDPC support *//* STBC support *//* 11n info *//* HT information *//* 11n beamforming *//* 2.4G band vht capabilities *//* 5G band capabilities *//* SCS related information *//* SCS (ACI/CCI Detection and Mitigation) workqueue *//* OCAC related information*//* Override OpMode Notification IE, for WFA Testbed *//* Enable fixed GI setting *//* Enable dynamic GI selection *//* Fixed bw setting *//* Default expansion matrices *//* Channel change due to noise at STA *//* Channel change due to noise at brcm STA *//* tx qos sched index for hold-time table *//* Use RTS on local node *//* Config for informing peer nodes to use RTS *//* Dynamic peer RTS current status *//* Inform peer nodes to use RTS *//* Dynamic WMM enabled *//* Deactive all DFS channels *//*
	 * Channel state:
	 *
	 * ic_channels is the set of available channels for the device;
	 *    it is setup by the driver
	 * ic_nchans is the number of valid entries in ic_channels
	 * ic_chan_avail is a bit vector of these channels used to check
	 *    whether a channel is available w/o searching the channel table.
	 * ic_chan_active is a (potentially) constrained subset of
	 *    ic_chan_avail that reflects any mode setting or user-specified
	 *    limit on the set of channels to use/scan
	 * ic_curchan is the current channel the device is set to; it may
	 *    be different from ic_bsschan when we are off-channel scanning
	 *    or otherwise doing background work
	 * ic_bsschan is the channel selected for operation; it may
	 *    be undefined (IEEE80211_CHAN_ANYC)
	 * ic_prevchan is a cached ``previous channel'' used to optimize
	 *    lookups when switching back+forth between two channels
	 *    (e.g. for dynamic turbo)
	 *//* RFIC chip ID *//* # entries in ic_channels *//* channel switch record *//* reason for the last channel switch *//* client mac addr when SCS channel switch *//* channel not used as primary *//* 0x1-regulatory 0x2-user override *//* channel is DFS required *//* weather radar channel *//* channels are disabled *//* BSS channel width, in station mode only *//* current channel *//* bss channel *//* previous channel *//* scanning channel *//* current channel noise in dBm *//* desired channel *//* Saved desired chan to switch after Initial CAC *//* Saved desired chan to switch after Initial Scan *//* desired mode *//* regulatory class ids *//* # entries in ic_regclassids *//* fast reassociate channel *//* Number of times tried to do fast reassoc *//* scan-related state *//* scan state *//* roaming mode *//* time of last data frame *//* time last scan completed *//* NB: this is the union of all vap stations/neighbors *//* stations/neighbors *//* XXX multi-bss: split out common/vap parts? *//* WME/WMM state *//* enable automatic adjusting wme bss param based on vap priority *//* airtime fairness *//* XXX multi-bss: can per-vap be done/make sense? *//* 802.11g protection mode *//* # non-ERP stations *//* # long slot time stations *//* total assoc limit per interface *//* stations associated(including WDS node) *//* WDS links created *//* dturbo capable stations *//* XR stations associated *//* Non-Quantenna peers *//* VAPs logical group assocication limits *//* dwell times for channel scanning *//* Adding Wireless stats per MAC. Per Vap is maintained in vap structure *//*
	 * Spectrum Management.
	 *//* specific country code for EU region *//* country info element *//* Supported operating class *//*
	 *  current channel power constraint for Power Constraint IE.
	 *
	 *  NB: local power constraint depends on the channel, but assuming it must
	 *     be detected dynamically, we cannot maintain a table (i.e., will not
	 *     know value until change to channel and detect).
	 *//* Power constraint override related information*//* last csa count *//* last csa mode *//* csa channel *//* Timer that is used to send CSA frame n number of times *//* last cca token *//* upcoming cca measurement *//* tsf at which cca measurement will occur *//* duration of cca measurement in TU *//* channel of cca measurement *//* if not zero jump to this channel if radar is detected *//* tracks best alternate chan to fast-switch into if radar is detected *//* radar non-occupancy period. *//* boot time CAC*//* virtual ap create/delete *//* send/recv 802.11 management frame *//* send an 802.11 encapsulated frame to the driver *//* reset device state after 802.11 parameter/state change *//* update device state for 802.11 slot time change *//* new station association callback/notification *//* node state management *//* scanning support *//* u-apsd support *//* set coverage class *//* mhz to ieee conversion *//* L2 external filter *//* Stats support *//* Change of the MIMO power save mode for the STA *//* TKIP MIC failure report *//* DFS radar detection handling *//* DFS radar selection function *//* DFS action when channel scan is done*//* Check if current region belongs to EU region *//* DFS select channel *//* tdls parameters configuration *//* Convert mcs to phy rate in Kbps *//* Count of the number of nodes allocated - for debug *//* Functions at sta to apply commands from AP *//* Callbacks at AP to send commands to sta *//* Callback to stream throttler external to vsp module *//* BA throttling for 3rd party client control *//* association ID bitmap *//* Number of pm intervals(interface with pm_interval module) *//* Compatibility fix with other vendor chipset *//* power management *//* CoC period change timer *//* for BMPS tput measurement *//* hold the calling task until the scan completes *//* Soc mac addr of the STB*//* Soc IP addr of the STB*//* tpc query info *//* measurement request *//*timer for detecting whether it is suitable to enable/disable AMPDU*//* WOWLAN related information *//* Extender role *//* MBS RSSI weight *//* RBS RSSI weight *//* MBS best RSSI threshold *//* MBS best RSSI threshold *//* EXTENDER Debug Level *//* MBS RSSI margin, used in link down detection only *//* record continuous RSSI event times *//* timer used by RBS to search MBS *//* recorded bandwidth of RBS *//* tqew desc limit *//* scan results expire timer *//* VHT related callbacks *//* 1 - enabled, 0 - disabled*//* Neighbor APs' count *//* Threshold of neighbor AP count when it's sparse *//* Threshold of neighbor AP count when it's dense *//* tx airtime callbacks *//* mu group update callback *//* sync rx reorder window on receiving BAR
	 * 0 - disabled
	 * 1 - enabled for QTN devices only
	 * 2 - enabled for all devices
	 *//* RecoveredOEM490per-radio state; existingmemberprefix remains intact. *//* OEM491 owns independent host PM policy/transaction state. *//* OEM449: prior padding. *//* Recovered OEM493 host-only state after inheritedCoC20byte state. *//* Recovered OEM492 NeighborReport advertisement state. *//* ts of rssi value from last read *//* 1 byte rssi value, 0 = threshold is off *//* 1 byte rssi value *//* buffer length *//* buffer containing one or more IEs *//* response parameters you expect *//* append differenet sub element data*//* Teardown counter of this TDLS link *//* Intervals that disable TDLS link *//**
 * Interworking Information
 *//* access network type *//* homogeneous essid *//*
 * Station profile specific to dual band mode.
 * Each band will maintain profile to be referred while band change.
