 **//*
 * The HGW-500BNA-QCv2 exposes its two Bootbase environments as read-only MTD
 * devices.  A target-gated early userspace importer validates both CRCs and
 * publishes only matching calibration records in tmpfs before qdrv loads.
 * Preserve the OEM MuC file-descriptor ABI while keeping normal builds on the
 * original /proc/bootcfg paths.
 *//*                          *//* IOCTL_HLINK_DEVATTACH    *//* IOCTL_HLINK_DEVDETACH    *//* IOCTL_HLINK_DEVCHANGE    *//* IOCTL_HLINK_LOGATTACH    *//* IOCTL_HLINK_TEMP_ATTACH   *//* IOCTL_HLINK_SVCERRATTACH *//* IOCTL_HLINK_RTNLEVENT    *//* IOCTL_HLINK_NDP_FRAME    *//* IOCTL_HLINK_FOPS_REQ  *//* IOCTL_HLINK_MIC_ERR *//* IOCTL_HLINK_BOOTED *//* IOCTL_HLINK_DROP_BA *//* IOCTL_HLINK_DISASSOC_STA *//* IOCTL_HLINK_RFIC_CAUSED_REBOOT *//* IOCTL_HLINK_BA_ADD_START *//* IOCTL_HLINK_PEER_RTS *//* IOCTL_HLINK_DYN_WMM *//* IOCTL_HLINK_TDLS_EVENTS	*//* IOCTL_HLINK_RATE_TRAIN	*//* argp is already a virtual address *//* clear the argp in the ioctl to prevent MuC from cleaning it up*//**
 * Message from MUC to qdriver indicating a number of TKIP MIC errors (as reported
 * by the MAC hardware).
 *
 * Pass this on to the WLAN driver to thence pass up to the higher layer to act on.
 *//* IOCTL argument 1 is:
	 * 31      24      16                    0
	 *  | RESVD | UNIT  |      DEVICE ID     |
	 *//* Currently only have a single MAC *//* "Parent" device *//* This used to call dev_open() on the parent device - not needed now *//* only have 1 WMAC *//* create_qdev() *//* Mark that we have successfully allocated a resource *//* Map temp index *//* Save the current status, in case the mode is changed *//* Initialisation *//* See if the hostlink address is setup *//* Take the semaphore *//* Get the contents of the message mailbox - physical address *//* Clear the content of the mailbox. *//* Translate to a local address. Can't do this earlier or
		 * we'd translate '0' to '0x80000000'
		 *//* Give back the semaphore *//* Call the right message handle function *//* If we have argp pointer, translate it *//* The message code indexes directly into the table *//* Put argp back *//* We don't have a handler for this message *//* Move to the next one *//* MBOX will be passed in by the MuC when it starts up *//* Finish the interrupt work in a workqueue *//* Install handler. Use mac device 0 *//* Make sure work queues are done *//**
