 **//*
 * Define boiler plate module stuff
 *//* 3.1 times seems safe for MuC (or AuC) crash - found by trial and error *//*
	* FIXME: return value should reflect failure if qdrv_control_input
	* above said so. And yet busybox echo seems to retry for failure.
	* This is not what we expected. Have to make it success here, while
	* what we really should fix is busybox echo
	*//* flag to trigger kernel panic on MuC halt isr *//* panic if appropriate - will eventually restart the system by calling machine_restart() *//* Must be less than the mproc timeout *//* service entry points and corresponding attributes for PHY stats entries in the sys fs *//*
	 * avoid buffer overruns ...
	 * i.e. for command "hexdump /sys/devices/qdrv/rssi_phy_stats",
	 * size is only 16.
	 *//* Get the size of our private data data structure *//* Allocate (zero filled) private memory for our device context *//* Attach the private memory to the device *//* device_register initialized the kobject even when add failed. *//* Initialize control interface *//* no cleanup and no error reporting required if failure *//* Last successful init step: no subsequent failure can unload a pin. *//* The retained kernel reference protects module text; this is a second guard. *//* Cleanup in reverse order *//* Only an unmutated instance can reach normal module exit. *//* Exit the control interface *//* Get the private device data *//* Free the private memory *//**
