 **//* valid only when Y is a power of 2, redefine more generally */// index : 0~76//=========20Mhz with long GI from MCS 0 ~ 15===============//20Mhz with long GI from MCS 16 ~ 31//20Mhz with long GI from MCS 32 ~ 47//20Mhz with long GI from MCS 48 ~ 63//20Mhz with long GI from MCS 64 ~ 76//==========20Mhz with short GI from MCS 0 ~ 15==============//20Mhz with short GI from MCS 16 ~ 31//20Mhz with short GI from MCS 32 ~ 47//20Mhz with short GI from MCS 48 ~ 63//20Mhz with short GI from MCS 64 ~ 76//======40Mhz with long GI from MCS 0 ~ 15==================//40Mhz with long GI from MCS 16 ~ 31//40Mhz with long GI from MCS 32 ~ 47//40Mhz with long GI from MCS 48 ~ 63//40Mhz with long GI from MCS 64 ~ 76//========40Mhz with short GI from MCS 0 ~ 15================//40Mhz with short GI from MCS 16 ~ 31//40Mhz with short GI from MCS 32 ~ 47//40Mhz with short GI from MCS 48 ~ 63//40Mhz with short GI from MCS 64 ~ 76/* rate in uint 100kbps *//* 20MHz, Long GI, Nss = 1, MCS 0 ~ 9 *//* 20MHz, Long GI, Nss = 2, MCS 0 ~ 9 *//* 20MHz, Long GI, Nss = 3, MCS 0 ~ 9 *//* 20MHz, Long GI, Nss = 4, MCS 0 ~ 9 *//* 20MHz, Short GI, Nss = 1, MCS 0 ~ 9 *//* 20MHz, Short GI, Nss = 2, MCS 0 ~ 9 *//* 20MHz, Short GI, Nss = 3, MCS 0 ~ 9 *//* 20MHz, Short GI, Nss = 4, MCS 0 ~ 9 *//* 40MHz, Long GI, Nss = 1, MCS 0 ~ 9 *//* 40MHz, Long GI, Nss = 2, MCS 0 ~ 9 *//* 40MHz, Long GI, Nss = 3, MCS 0 ~ 9 *//* 40MHz, Long GI, Nss = 4, MCS 0 ~ 9 *//* 40MHz, Short GI, Nss = 1, MCS 0 ~ 9 *//* 40MHz, Short GI, Nss = 2, MCS 0 ~ 9 *//* 40MHz, Short GI, Nss = 3, MCS 0 ~ 9 *//* 40MHz, Short GI, Nss = 4, MCS 0 ~ 9 *//* 80MHz, Long GI, Nss = 1, MCS 0 ~ 9 *//* 80MHz, Long GI, Nss = 2, MCS 0 ~ 9 *//* 80MHz, Long GI, Nss = 3, MCS 0 ~ 9 *//* 80MHz, Long GI, Nss = 4, MCS 0 ~ 9 *//* 80MHz, Short GI, Nss = 1, MCS 0 ~ 9 *//* 80MHz, Short GI, Nss = 2, MCS 0 ~ 9 *//* 80MHz, Short GI, Nss = 3, MCS 0 ~ 9 *//* 80MHz, Short GI, Nss = 4, MCS 0 ~ 9 *//* 160MHz, Long GI, Nss = 1, MCS 0 ~ 9 *//* 160MHz, Long GI, Nss = 2, MCS 0 ~ 9 *//* 160MHz, Long GI, Nss = 3, MCS 0 ~ 9 *//* 160MHz, Long GI, Nss = 4, MCS 0 ~ 9 *//* 160MHz, Short GI, Nss = 1, MCS 0 ~ 9 *//* 160MHz, Short GI, Nss = 2, MCS 0 ~ 9 *//* 160MHz, Short GI, Nss = 3, MCS 0 ~ 9 *//* 160MHz, Short GI, Nss = 4, MCS 0 ~ 9 *//* Tag to filter(grep) statistics in csv format *//* The returned rate has unit kbps *//*
 * Display RSSI/EVM stats of the node with the most packets
 *//* RSSIs in dBM (units are actually 0.1 dBM) ... *//* RSSIs in dBM (units are actually 0.1 dBM) ... */// doing the dB summation/* New line *//* Comma to separate linux time stamp *//*
 * Possible values for required_phy_stat_mode are defined in include/qtn/muc_phy_stats.h
 * They define the possible phy stats mode in the ieee80211com.  As the parameter
 * required_phy_stat_mode the meaning of the values is:
 *
 *      MUC_PHY_STATS_ALTERNATE		- any block will do, so return the latest
 *      MUC_PHY_STATS_RSSI_RCPI_ONLY	- block must have RSSIs and RCPI, not errored sums
 *      MUC_PHY_STATS_ERROR_SUM_ONLY	- block must have errored sums, not RSSIs or RCPIs.
 *//*
 * If required_phy_stat_mode is MUC_PHY_STATS_RSSI_RCPI_ONLY or MUC_PHY_STATS_ERROR_SUM_ONLY,
 * none of the blocks may have what is required (based on the current phy stats mode in the
 * ieee80211com).  If so, return NULL.
 *//*
 * Parse log is subtly different from get address latest stats.
 *
 *     Parse Log reports ALL stats that have not been previously reported;
 *     thus it uses a file-scope variable "last_tstamp" to track which
 *     stats have not been reported.  If called repeatedly between MUC
 *     updates it returns without reporting anything.
 *
 *     Get Address Latest Stats returns the address of the stats with the
 *     latest time stamp.  It can thus be repeatedly called between updates
 *     from the MUC, with each call in this situation returning the address
 *     of the same qtn_stats.
 *//* Display header periodically *//*
 * These functions need to be prepared for qtn_muc_stats_get_addr_latest_stats returning NULL.
 *
 * Currently they all return -1 to signal Failed to Get Requested Value.
 *//* RSSIs in dBM (units are actually 0.1 dBM) ... *//**
