 * Set a per-node threshold for packets queued to the MuC, based on the number of associated nodes,
 * including WDS nodes.
 * PERNODE_TBD - all WDS nodes should count as one under the current scheme
 *//* Increase the reference count of the VAP netdev *//* ignore channels that do not match the required bandwidth *//* ignore channels where radar has been detected *//* store normal txpower for short range workaround *//* FIXME: Disabling MODE changes for now *//* Fixme : Do proper support for STA scan on MuC *//* FIXME: Disabling MODE changes for now *//* Fixme : Do proper support for STA scan on MuC *//*
	 * These frames are inserted into the tx datapath on the MuC, not in qdrv.
	 * The node ID is unset in order to avoid multiple node free operations during tx_done.
	 *//*
 * qdrv_bmps_release_frame: release the null frame queued in sp->bmps_lhost
 * return 0: succeed; -1: failed
 *//*
 * qdrv_bmps_set_frame: set the frame to sp->bmps_lhost
 * NOTE: MUST be called with a reference to the node entry within
 * the SKB CB structure, and free the reference to the node entry
 * after this calling.
 * return 0: succeed; -1: faild, need free skb by the caller.
 *//*
         * Release the previous null frame if it has not been released,
         * and then get one new tx descriptor
         *//*
 * qdrv_scs_release_frame: release the qosnull frame queued in sp->chan_sample_lhost
 * return 0: succeed; -1: failed
 *//*
 * qdrv_scs_set_frame: set the frame to sp->chan_sample_lhost
 * return 0: succeed; -1: failed.
 *//*
	 * Release the previous qosnull frame if it has not been released,
	 * and then get one new tx descriptor
	 *//* set qosnull frame *//* check the airtime of this bss *//* check the packet number in tx queue *//* QTN_BG_SCAN *//* sample channel not allowed in power-saving mode *//* indicate sample channel is on-going *//* QSCS_ENABLED *//*
 * qdrv_bgscan_start: reset bgscan status if it is not idle or completed
 * return 0: succeed; -1: failed
 *//*
 * qdrv_bgscan_release_frame: delete the frame queued in sp->chan_scan_lhost
 * return 0: succeed; -1: failed
 *//*
 * qdrv_bgscan_set_frame: set the frame to sp->chan_scan_lhost
 * NOTE: MUST be called with a reference to the node entry within
 * the SKB CB structure, and free the reference to the node entry
 * after this calling.
 * return 0: succeed; -1: faild, need free skb by the caller.
 *//* set start frame *//* set probe request frame *//* QTN_BG_SCAN *//*
 * deferred channel change, where the MuC handles the channel change,
 * aiming to change at a particular tsf, and notifies the lhost when it occurs.
 *//*
		 * the muc may pick this up, but if it doesn't it will
		 * complete the entire channel change
		 *//* csa in progress *//* Time Units *//* mark the entire process as done *//* clear csa count at last to avoid any possibility of dual CS *//* indicate sample channel is done *//* start power-saving if allowed *//* just switched channel, restart radar *//* all done! *//* call workqueue to handle callback *//* successfully cancelled *//* indicate sample channel is done *//* start power-saving if allowed *//*
	 * TODO SCS: radar disable during the cca read
	 *//* QTN_BG_SCAN *//*
 * Set the qosnull frame to sp->ocac_lhost
 * NOTE: MUST be called with a reference to the node entry within
 * the SKB CB structure, and free the reference to the node entry
 * after this call.
 * Return 0 for success or -1 on failure.
 * If failed, skb must be freed by the caller.
 *//* start ocac in MuC *//* Set qosnull frame *//* stop ocac in MuC *//*
 * disable radar detection and tx queue,
 * trigger a cca read to start.
 * returns 0 if a cca read ioctl was sent to the MuC successfully,
 * < 0 if we are currently performing a cca read or other error
 *//* sample channel not allowed in power-saving mode *//*
	 * TODO SCS: radar.
	 *//* indicate sample channel is on-going *//*
 * The OEM v37.4.0.89 module exports the same implementation under the older
 * qdrv_async_cca_read name.  Keep both names: this is an additive symbol ABI
 * bridge and does not change the shared-memory or call ABI.
 *//* channel 0 means current channel *//* QTN_BG_SCAN *//* sample channel not allowed in power-saving mode *//* indicate sample channel is on-going *//* NOTE: the number of records cannot dynamically change or buffer overflow may happen *//*
				 * Re-cache the index - it may have changed by this point, if alloc above
				 * takes a while.
				 *//* Just in case re-enable rx interrupts *//*
 * Transmit an 802.11 encapped management or data frame via the management path.
 * This function must be called with a reference to the node structure.
 *//* Automatic install of BA *//* By default put a STA in VLAN 1 *//*
 *  Process setkey request
 *//* Copy the values over *//*
 *  Process delkey request
 *//* Copy the values over *//*
 *  Process addba request
 *//*
 * Send addba request
 *//* This is to inform qdrv scheduler that better AC may have worse parameter settings *//* Automatic install of BA *//* allocate or free/re-allocate null frame *//* Network is operating in 40 MHZ mode *//* Network is operating in 20 MHZ mode *//* This is an 11AC network *//* Publish only after the final v89 wire image is visible to MuC. *//* The normal send path has already returned the slot to hostlink. *//*
 *  Process delba request
 *//* Copy the values over *//*
 *  Enter/Leave power save state on STA mode
 *//* For Spatial stream from 1-8; set MCS=3 (not supported) *//* At least 1 spatial stream supported *//*
	 * phymode has already been initialized through set_bw
	 * - need to reinitialize if in 11ac mode
	 *//* Configure beacon interval to power duty interval *//* pass through, let the rts threshold value packed as normal param below *//*
			 * Turn off BF capabilities in the beacon when bfoff. Should
			 * work for both AP beamformer and STA beamformee disabling
			 * when bfoff is set.
			 * *//*
			 * In Amber WOWLAN is handled by WIFI2SOC interrupt.
			 *//* Make sure the data fits if it is provided *//* Copy the values over *//* place the sta's mac addr at the end of its group/pos arrays *//*
		 * PCIE TQE port is determined at runtime
		 *//*
 * This function performs proxy ARP for 3-address stations.  It is intended for use
 * with HS 2.0 vaps, which do not support 4-address stations.
 *//*
		 * If the ARP announcement came from an associated station,
		 * update the node's IP address.
		 *//* type(1byte) + len(1byte) + Dev addr len + pad *//* Duplicate address detection *//* send multicast neighbour advertisement frame to back end only *//* send unicast neighbour advertisement frame to STA *//* Verify unsolicited neighbour advertisement *//* OEM read-only getters331/275 use these existing named fields.
	 * The port compiler ABI witness is independent of OEM numeric offsets. *//*
	 * NB: the referenced node pointer is in the
	 * control block of the sk_buff.  This is
	 * placed there by ieee80211_mgmt_output because
	 * we need to hold the reference with the frame.
	 *//* Get the data from MuC *//* No stats available from MuC, mark all as invalid *//* Take the previous value *//* Collect error stats *//*
	 * Collect PHY Stats
	 *
	 * The RSSI values reported in the TX/RX descriptors in the driver are the SNR
	 * expressed in dBm. Thus 'rssi' is signal level above the noise floor in dBm.
	 *
	 * Noise is measured in dBm and is negative unless there is an unimaginable
	 * level of RF noise.
	 *
	 * The signal level is noise + rssi.
	 *
	 * Note that the iw_quality values are 1 byte, and can be signed, unsigned or
	 * negative depending on context.
         *
         * Note iwconfig's quality parameter is a relative value while rssi here is a
         * absolute/dBm value.
         * Convert rssi from absolute/dBm value to a relative one.
         * The convertion logic is reused from qcsapi
	 *//*
 * MIMO power save mode change.
 *//* BSSID for the node and it's MAC address *//* new_mode is one of the enumerations starting 'IEEE80211_HTCAP_C_MIMOPWRSAVE_...' *//* List of bridge clients *//* List of Quantenna bridge clients that support 4-addr LNCB reception *//* Don't count this STA more than once. Can happen when reauthenticating *//* check if channel requires DFS *//* active scan not allowed on DFS channel *//* qdrv_pm_notify is registered in qos_pm framework *//* it could be triggered from modules besides wlan qdrv: e.g. qpm *//* so we need to make sure BMPS is enabled *//* before going into power-saving in STA mode *//* BMPS power-saving is used for STA *//* this is only needed for CoC power-saving in non-STA mode *//* Configure beacon interval to power duty interval *//* Recovering beacon setting *//* Set up some dummy channels *//* Dual band. Initialize with all the supported channels *//* Add the common 40M flag if either U/D 20M flag is set *//* '0' means power is not configured *//* Add the common 40M flag if either U/D 20M flag is set *//* '0' means power is not configured *//* Add the common 40M flag if either U/D 20M flag is set *//* '0' means power is not configured *//* check if channel requires DFS *//* Initialize the channels in the ieee80211com structure *//* Disable STA side control for QTM-Lite *//* Disable STA side control for QTM-Lite *//*
 * VSP config callback to send a configuration updates to peer stations
 *//* Store config for sending to new stations when they associate *//*
 * VSP config callback to send stream state changes to peer stations
 *//*
			 * There is a race condition that when lhost is reading these counters from
			 * shared memory, MuC is updating it. However, this won't hurt VSP. Because
			 * the key information here is whether throt_pkts is zero or not. We rely
			 * on this when reenabling streams. The small error in sent_pkts doesn't
			 * matter. So we don't need to use ping-pong buffer to solve this race condtion.
			 *//* sched work one time less than interval number because here we already do one *//* warming up, stats not ready yet *//* default interval *//* ms *//* bytes *//* bool, whether to throt session duration *//* bool, whether to throt winsize *//* must be first entry *//* more entries can be dynamically added *//*
 * Manually control BA throttling instead of VSP automatic control
 *//* apply it to all vap as we don't support per-vap wme params now *//*
 * Manually control WME throttling instead of VSP automatic control
 *//* CONFIG_QVSP *//*
	 * Workaround for transfer across slow ethernet interfaces (100Mbps or less)
	 * Reduce advertised RX MAX AMPDU to reduce sender hold time
	 * Reduce TX aggr hold time (done in MuC)
	 *//* Highest advertised rate is supported *//*
	 * Not yet supported:
	 *   IEEE80211_VHTCAP_C_SHORT_GI_160
	 *   IEEE80211_VHTCAP_C_VHT_TXOP_PS
	 *//* revisit *//* revisit *//* revisit *//* revisit *//* Not supported in current BBIC4 hardware *//* QDRV_FEATURE_VHT *//* If radar found and non-occupancy started, mark all sub-channels as radar found *//*
					 * Mark primary channel and subchannels as CAC_DONE,
					 * to prevent CAC being run when set channel is issued
					 * on one of the sub-channels.
					 *//*
					 * Non-Occupancy expired; Mark the channels as ready for cac
					 * Once non-occupancy is period is expired, we should be able to do
					 * CAC on the channel;
					 *//* If radar found and non-occupancy started, mark all sub-channels as radar found *//*
					 * Mark primary channel and subchannels as CAC_DONE,
					 * to prevent CAC being run when set channel is issued
					 * on one of the sub-channels.
					 *//*
					 * Non-Occupancy expired; Mark the channels as ready for cac
					 * Once non-occupancy is period is expired, we should be able to do
					 * CAC on the channel
					 *//**
 * @function : qdrv_dfs_chans_available_for_cac
 * @param    : ieee80211_channel [ch]: check if this channel is ready for CAC.
 *		if [ch] is NULL, function returns true if any one channel is ready for CAC
 * @brief    : returns true if atleast one DFS channel is found for which
 *		cac not yet done
 *//* Check channel ch is ready for CAC *//* Update the boot time CAC timestamp only when ICAC is actually in-progress *//* set the max_boot_cac_duration to -1 *//* Stop on-going ICAC timer if any *//*
				 * AP operation and we already have a channel;
				 * bypass the scan and startup immediately.
				 * But under repeater mode, initiate the AP scan anyway
				 *//* To bypass chan check against curr chan while validating channel *//*
				 * When max_boot_cac timer is too large value, and no channels left for CAC
				 * stop the ICAC procedure
				 *//* Set up some dummy channels *//* Initialize the ieee80211com structure *//* These are called without protection from 802.11 layer *//* Hook up our code *//* Hook up our Block ack code *//* Hook up our Security code *//* Hook up the MIMO power save mode change *//* Function to authorize/deauthorize an STA *//* Station has joined or rejoined a BSS *//* Hoop up to set the TDLS parameters *//* Should set real opmode here - not just a placeholder *//* ibss, nee adhoc, mode *//* hostap mode *//* monitor mode *//* adhoc demo mode *//* short preamble supported *//* short slot time supported *//* capable of WPA1 + WPA2 *//* WMM/WME *//* Capable of Tx Power Management *//* Capable of unequal modulation *//* Capable of background scan *//* Capable of WMM power save*//* ms *//* for WFA testbed *//* Assign the mac address *//* Call MI attach routine. *//* defaults for SCS *//* QSCS_ENABLED *//* QTN_BG_SCAN *//* we don't have short range issue with Topaz *//* initiate data struct that record channel switch *//* tx airtime callback init *//* MU group state update *//* QTN_BG_SCAN *//*
 * If BIT(24) is set, it stands for all nodes.
 * If not, 8 LSBs stands for the node index.
 * BIT(8)-BIT(15) stands for the control masks.
 *//*
	 * Client creation can succeed even if the device's probe callback failed,
	 * so check that the temperature sensor is functional.
	 *//*
		 * If no external temp sensor is found then rx_stats sys_temp
		 * would be updated from internal temp sensor
		 *//*
	 * The OEM userspace creates wifi0 almost immediately after core start.
	 * The instrumented Linux 5.10 ladder is intentionally slower, so this
	 * timer can expire before MuC owns a VAP device.  SET_HRFLAGS then makes
	 * the .89 MuC dereference its null device at +0x3c.  Preserve hang
	 * recovery, but defer the one-shot until the first VAP is attached.
	 *//* Enable the one-shot timer to enable hang detection/recovery *//* Stop the MuC so we can borrow its stack *//* Hook into the troubleshoot functions *//* Old struct qnet_priv *//* Allocate a wlan structure *//* Clean it out *//* Store it in the mac structure as opaque private data *//* We need the back pointer so we can control interrupts *//* Initialize the wlan data structure *//* init csa workqueues and irq handlers *//* QTN_BG_SCAN *//* Initialize the TX interface *//* Initialize the RX interface *//* Initialize the Scan interface *//* Initialize the hostlink interface *//* Initialize the beamforming support *//* Start the RX interface *//* Start the TX interface *//* Start the Scan interface *//* Start the hostlink interface *//* Set up rate tables for all potential media types. *//* Initialize the 802.11 layer (old qtn_attach()) *//* start DFS function *//* Timer to enable hang recovery. We delay this as the intial channel
	 * change can take a long time to complete, causing false hangs to be
	 * detected.
	 *//* Subscribe to PM notifications *//* WPS Polling programs *//* qdrv_soc_exit() has physically stopped MuC before WLAN teardown. *//* Reset the MAC data structure *//*
* Queue of processes who access wps_button file
*//* WPS button event reported to user space process *//* As usual, this read is always blocked untill wps button is pressed
	 * so increase the module reference to prevent it being unload during
	 * blocking read
	 *//* wait for valid WPS button event *//* read back empty string in signal wakeup case *//* after new event been handled, reset to none event *//* dev_attr_wps_button *//* records the jiffies when button down, back to 0 after button released *//* timer internal *//* records the falling edge jiffies *//* at rising edge *//* WPS button event is rising triggered -- when button
		 * being changed from active to inactive level.
		 *
		 * Different press time trigger different event
		 *//* wakeup the event waiting processes *//* wakeup the event waiting processes *//* back to 0 after rising edge *//* Restart the timer *//*
	 * Set up timer to poll the button.
	 * Request the GPIO resource and export it for userspace
	 *//* creeate the device file for user space use *//* current wps button is in released state, so its value can determine active_logic *//**
