 * Country Code Table for code-to-string conversion.
 *//* Make sure the global class entry must be the last one *//* {band_chan_step, band_first_chan, band_chan_cnt} *//* isolate chan 165 for IOT as per sniffer capture *//*******************************************************************************//* ieee80211_sta_bmps_update: allocate, re-allocate or free BMPS NULL frame    *//*                                                                             *//* NOTE: this function should be called whenever a new assocation              *//*       happens, because node id associated with the frame needs              *//*       to be updated                                                         *//*******************************************************************************//* set null frame *//* free null frame *//* Checking non-sta mode for WDS link *//* here is the logic which decide should power-save or not *//* multiple VAPS, and one of them is STA *//* force power-saving off *//* for single STA VAP: mark as idle only if *//* 1. BMPS power-saving is enabled, and *//* 2. not in SCAN process, and *//* 3. not in SCS sample channel process, and *//* 4. no beacon missing warning *//* manual mode *//* auto mode *//* and tput is low *//************************************************************//* ieee80211_bmps_tput_check: calculate TX/RX tput          *//*                                                          *//* NOTE: this tput information will be used to decide       *//*       entering/exiting power-saving state automatically  *//*       while BMPS works in AUTO mode                      *//************************************************************//* get VAP TX/RX bytes stats info *//* calculate overall TX & RX tput *//* over the past measuring period *//* tput is above upper threshold *//* it is time to exit BMPS power-saving *//* tput is below lower threshold *//* it is time to enter BMPS power-saving *//* Recovered OEM491 PM/CSA consumer, analysis entries 0x83da0/0x83f28/
 * 0x84028. Host state is separate from channel-switch diagnostics. The sole
 * consumed PM-trigger distinction is node-join13 versus every other reason.
 * Invalid/ANYC BSS pointers are explicitly refused instead of OEM dereference.
 * Existing channel validation and CSA completion remain authoritative. *//* Timer context cannot call the mutex/blocking-notifier QoS provider.
     * Preserve the sampled pre-completion PM level until process work runs. *//* Existing provider is cancel_delayed_work_sync. Producers are gated
     * before cancellation; teardown then joins the preexisting CSA timer. *//* Consume one actual producer request before publishing completion.
     * A producer arriving later owns a newly queued run and stays pending. *//* The OEM worker accesses BSS flags before an invalid-pointer check.
     * Avoid changing QoS, pick state or callback ownership when not ready. *//*
	 * Pick an initial operating mode until we have a vap
	 * created to lock it down correctly.  This is only
	 * drivers have something defined for configuring the
	 * hardware at startup.
	 *//* everyone supports this *//*
	 * Fill in 802.11 available channel set, mark
	 * all available channels as active, and pick
	 * a default channel if not already specified.
	 *//* make sure only valid 2.4G or 5G channels are set as available *//*
		 * Identify mode capabilities.
		 *//* initialize candidate channels to all available *//* validate ic->ic_curmode *//*
	 * When 11g is supported, force the rate set to
	 * include basic rates suitable for a mixed b/g bss.
	 *//* 11n also checks for 11g basic rates for capabilities *//* setup initial channel settings *//* arbitrarily pick the first channel *//* Enable marking of dfs by default *//* Phytype OFDM. FIXME: this may change with RFIC5 *//* Enable LDPC by default *//*
	 * Enable WME by default if we're capable.
	 *//* default 7 beacons *//* AP support tdls and STA disable tdls by default *//*
	 * The caller is assumed to allocate the device with
	 * alloc_etherdev or similar so we arrange for the
	 * space to be reclaimed accordingly.
	 *//* back pointer *//* propagate common flags *//* Default Multicast traffic to lowest rate of 1000 Kbps*//* Enabling short GI by default. This may be right place to set it *//* Initialize vht capability flags  *//* Disable STBC by default  *//* WDS/Repeater *//* do DBS specific initialization, keep it open for all chipset,
		 * as we don't want chip specific execution here, for RF with no
		 * dual band support, these initiazation won't be referenced.
		 *//* 2,4ghz specific station profile *//* 5ghz specific station profile *//* Set WDS according to Extender Role *//*
	 * Enable various functionality by default if we're capable.
	 *//* Defaults for implicit BA and global BA mask *//* initialize TDLS Function *//* Only need the peer entry in AID table for WDS mode VAP *//* NB: defer setting dev_addr so driver can override *//* exactOEM484VAPsetupdefault *//* XXX move into vattach *//* XXX move into vattach *//* Fix issue that tx power will be abnormal when dynamically switch from station mode to AP mode*//* NB: rtnl is held on entry so don't use register_netdev *//* reset to supported mode *//*
	 * Change state to 'INIT' to disassociate WDS peer node
	 *//* NB: rtnl is held on entry so don't use unregister_netdev *//*
 * Convert MHz frequency to IEEE channel number.
 *//* 2GHz band *//* Japan *//* don't number non-IEEE channels *//* 5Ghz band *//* don't number non-IEEE channels *//* something is fishy, don't do anything *//*
 * Convert channel to IEEE channel number.
 *//*
 * Convert IEEE channel number to MHz frequency.
 *//* 2GHz band *//* 5Ghz band *//* either, guess *//* 0-13 *//* 15-26 *//*
 * Locate a channel given a frequency+flags.  We cache
 * the previous lookup to optimize swithing between two
 * channels--as happens with dynamic turbo.
 *//* brute force search *//* &&
