 *//*
 * IEEE 802.11 beacon handling routines
 *//*
 * Add the Epigram IE to a frame
 *//* XXX timestamp is set by hardware/driver *//* beacon interval *//* capability information *//* ssid *//*
	 * Which mode AP is operating in? 20 MHz or 20/40 Mhz.
	 * Needs to know to put correct channel no in beacon
	 *//* supported rates *//* adding ELEMENTID_IBSSPARAMS or ELEMENTID_TIM here *//* IBSS/TIM *//*
	 * Tight coupling between Country IE and Power Constraint IE
	 * Both using IEEE80211_FEXT_COUNTRYIE to optional enable them.
	 *//* country *//* admissionrefused:noadvertisementpointer *//* BSS load element *//* Power constraint *//* Transmit power envelope *//*TPC Report*//* Channel Switch Announcement *//* Secondary Channel Offset *//* Ext. Supp. Rates *//* WME *//* WPA 1+2 *//* Can have VHT mode with 40MHz bandwidth *//* Wide Bandwidth Channel Switch *//* Channel Siwtch Wrapper *//* athAdvCaps *//* Extender IE *//* QTN WME IE *//* Add epigram IE to address interop issue with Gen 1 (other vendor) STB *//* XR *//* CCA info *//*
 * Allocate a beacon frame and fillin the appropriate bits.
 *//*
	 * beacon frame format
	 *	[8] time stamp
	 *	[2] beacon interval
	 *	[2] capability information
	 *	[tlv] ssid
	 *	[tlv] supported rates
	 *	[7] FH/DS parameter set
	 *	[tlv] IBSS/TIM parameter set
	 *	[tlv] country code
	 *	[3] power constraint
	 *	[5] channel switch announcement
	 *	[4] TPC Report
	 *	[3] extended rate phy (ERP)
	 *	[tlv] extended supported rates
	 *	[tlv] WME parameters
	 *	[tlv] WPA/RSN parameters
	 *	[tlv] HT Capabilities
	 *	[tlv] HT Information
	 *	[tlv] Atheros Advanced Capabilities
	 *	[tlv] AtherosXR parameters
	 *	[tlv] Quantenna flags
	 *	[tlv] epigram
	 * NB: we allocate the max space required for the TIM bitmap.
	 *//* time stamp *//* beacon interval *//* capability information *//* ssid *//* supported rates *//* FH/DS parameters max(7,3) *//* IBSS/TIM parameter set*//* country code *//* BSS load *//* power constraint *//* tpc report *//* channel switch announcement *//* ERP *//* Ext. Supp. Rates *//* WPA 1+2 *//* RecoveredRRMIE70 descriptor reserve *//*
 * Update the dynamic parts of a beacon frame based on the current state.
 *//* Dynamic extents must match the current unpublished frame before writes. *//* XXX faster to recalculate entirely or just changes? *//*
		 * Check for aggressive mode change.  When there is
		 * significant high priority traffic in the BSS
		 * throttle back BE traffic by using conservative
		 * parameters.  Otherwise BE uses aggressive params
		 * to optimize performance of legacy/non-QoS traffic.
		 *//* XXX multi-bss *//*
			 * Only update the content without changing length, descriptor is
			 * already queued
			 *//* Only update the content without changing length, descriptor is already queued *//* NB: no IBSS support*//*
		 * TIM IE is programmed in QTN FW hence code to manupulate TIM is removed
		*//* Change the CCA payload once, then reuse its reserved descriptor.
         * Move a following APP payload before inserting/removing CCA bytes. *//* Detach both old extents before their payload positions move. *//* Preserve original repeated-allocation algorithm. *//* queue cca IE at first place *//* FIXME ADM: not used should remove them.*//* if it is a mode change beacon for dynamic turbo case. *//* Already queued, update the content only so no need to add descriptor *//* APP payload replacement uses one reserved slot, including removal. *//* Preserve original APP allocation algorithm. *//* adjust the buffer size if the size is changed *//* update the trailer lens *//**
