 *//*
 * IEEE 802.11i TKIP crypto support.
 *
 * Part of this module is derived from similar code in the Host
 * AP driver. The code is used with the consent of the author and
 * it's license is included below.
 *//* for diagnostics + statistics *//* XXX for test module; make locals? *//* XXX for test module; make locals? *//* held until MIC verified *//* XXX *//* TSC starts at 1 *//*
 * Add privacy headers and do any s/w encryption required.
 *//*
	 * Handle TKIP counter measures requirement.
	 *//*
	 * Copy down 802.11 header and add the IV, KeyID, and ExtIV.
	 *//* TSC1 *//* WEP seed *//* TSC0 *//* KeyID | ExtID *//* TSC2 *//* TSC3 *//* TSC4 *//* TSC5 *//*
	 * Finally, do software encrypt if neeed.
	 *//* NB: tkip_encrypt handles wk_keytsc *//*
 * Add MIC to the frame as needed.
 *//* NB: should not happen *//* XXX statistic *//*
 * Validate and strip privacy headers (and trailer) for a
 * received frame.  If necessary, decrypt the frame using
 * the specified key.
 *//*
	 * Header should have extended IV and sequence number;
	 * verify the former and validate the latter.
	 *//*
		 * No extended IV; discard frame.
		 *//*
	 * Handle TKIP counter measures requirement.
	 *//*
		 * Replay violation; notify upper layer.
		 *//*
	 * NB: We can't update the rsc in the key until MIC is verified.
	 *
	 * We assume we are not preempted between doing the check above
	 * and updating wk_keyrsc when stripping the MIC in tkip_demic.
	 * Otherwise we might process another packet and discard it as
	 * a replay.
	 *//*
	 * Check if the device handled the decrypt in hardware.
	 * If so we just strip the header; otherwise we need to
	 * handle the decrypt in software.
	 *//*
	 * Copy up 802.11 header and strip crypto bits.
	 *//*
 * Verify and strip MIC from the frame.
 *//* NB: skb left pointing at last in chain *//* XXX assert skb->len >= tkip.ic_miclen *//* NB: 802.11 layer handles statistic and debug msg *//*
	 * Strip MIC from the tail.
	 *//*
	 * Ok to update rsc now that MIC has been verified.
	 *//*
 * Host AP crypt: host-based TKIP encryption implementation for Host AP driver
 *
 * Copyright (c) 2003-2004, Jouni Malinen <jkmaline@cc.hut.fi>
 *
 * This program is free software; you can redistribute it and/or modify
 * it under the terms of the GNU General Public License version 2 as
 * published by the Free Software Foundation. See README and COPYING for
 * more details.
 *
 * Alternatively, this software may be distributed under the terms of BSD
 * license.
 *//* Initialize the 80-bit TTAK from TSC (IV32) and TA[0..5] *//* Make temporary area overlap WEP seed so that the final copy can be
	 * avoided on little endian hosts. *//* Step 1 - make copy of TTAK and bring in TSC *//* Step 2 - 96-bit bijective mixing using S-box *//* Step 3 - bring in last of TK bits, assign 24-bit WEP IV value
	 * WEPSeed[0..2] is transmitted as WEP IV *//* Setup RC4 state *//* Compute CRC32 over unencrypted data and apply RC4 to data *//* Append little-endian CRC32 and encrypt it to produce ICV *//* Setup RC4 state *//* Apply RC4 to data and compute CRC32 over decrypted data *//* XXX msg? stat? cannot happen? *//* Encrypt little-endian CRC32 and verify that it matches with the
	 * received ICV *//* ICV mismatch - drop frame *//*
 * Craft pseudo header used to calculate the MIC.
 *//* DA *//* DA *//* DA *//* DA *//* reserved *//* Michael MIC pseudo header: DA, SA, 3 x 0, Priority *//* first buffer has special handling *//* collect 32-bit blocks from current buffer *//*
			 * Block straddles buffers, split references.
			 *//*
			 * Setup for next buffer.
			 *//* Last block and padding (0x5a, 4..7 x 0) *//* l ^= 0; *//* NB: should not happen *//* XXX statistic *//* NB: tkip_decap already verified header and left seq in rx_rsc *//* NB: skb is unstripped; deduct headers + ICV to get payload *//* Previously cached Phase1 result was already lost, so
			 * it needs to be recalculated for the next packet. *//*
 * Module glue.
 *//*-
