	 *//* setup the table *//* [1] is NULL terminator *//* XXX bad idea? *//* [3] is NULL terminator *//* copy in pre-defined data *//* add in dynamic data references *//* XXX? *//* and register everything *//* Ensure the base madwifi directory exists *//* Create a proc directory named after the VAP *//* Create a proc entry listing the associated stations *//* Recreate any other proc entries that have been registered *//* Frees all memory used for the list of proc entries *//* Called by other modules to register a proc entry under the vap directory *//* Ignore if already in the list *//* Check for end of list *//* Otherwise move on *//* Create an item in our list for the new entry *//* Create the entry record *//* Create the actual proc entry *//* Add it to the list *//* Add to the start *//* Add to the end *//* Remove child proc entries but leave them in the list *//*
 * Format an Ethernet MAC for printing.
