 * Send a probe request frame with the specified ssid
 * and any optional information element data.
 *//* Send a broadcast CSA frame, announcing the new channel. References are from
 * IEEE 802.11h-2003. CSA frame format is an "Action" frame (Type: 00, Subtype:
 * 1101, see 7.1.3.1.2)
 *
 * [1] Category : 0, Spectrum Management, 7.3.1.11
 * [1] Action : 4, Channel Switch Announcement, 7.4.1 and 7.4.1.5
 * [1] Element ID : 37, Channel Switch Announcement, 7.3.2
 * [1] Length : 3, 7.3.2.20
 * [1] Channel Switch Mode : 1, stop transmission immediately
 * [1] New Channel Number
 * [1] Channel Switch Count in TBTT : 0, immediate channel switch
 *
 * csa_mode : IEEE80211_CSA_CAN_STOP_TX / IEEE80211_CSA_MUST_STOP_TX
 * csa_chan : new IEEE channel number
 * csa_tbtt : TBTT until Channel Switch happens
*//* Category *//* Spectrum Management *//* STA mode - tell AP to change channel *//* Common header *//* Set state for one or more streams *//* Common header *//* Zero or more config index/value pairs. *//* measurement report filed would not exist if any bit of measurement report is set *//* optional sub element length *//* will be filled when finished *//* measurement token *//* mode *//* optional sub element *//* replace with real type *//* TODO: operating class, figure out a correct mapping *//* TODO: operating class, figure out a correct mapping *//* common part *//* fill the content here *//* fill the sta tx statistics *//* fill the sta rx statistics *//* fill the sta parameters *//* Vendor specific content: tlv length field *//* Vendor specific content: tlv length field *//* Vendor specific content: tlv length field *//* Vendor specific content: tlv length field *//* Vendor specific content: tlv length field *//* Vendor specific content: tlv length field *//* Vendor specific content: tlv length field *//* Vendor specific content: tlv length field *//* Vendor specific content: tlv length field *//* Vendor specific content: tlv length field *//* Reserved for cca *//* Vendor specific content: tlv length field *//* Vendor specific content: tlv length field *//* unkown type report 0 *//* Vendor specific content: tlv length field *//* reset all counter *//* Vendor specific content: tlv length field *//* reset all counter *//* Vendor specific content: tlv length field *//* replace with real type *//* qtn SCS IE *//* set number of repetitions to 0 *//* 4 anntenna, add 6 db *//*
 * To check whether to enable RX AMSDU or not.
 * Return 1: RX AMSDU can be enabled, 0: should be disabled
 *//*
 * Send a management frame.  The node is for the destination (or ic_bss
 * when in station mode).  Nodes other than ic_bss have their reference
 * count bumped to reflect our use for an indeterminate time.
 *//*
		 * In Roaming cases, STA may receive null data frames from old AP
		 * if it's not disassociated properly.
		 * We add a exception here so that STA can send De-auth to old AP.
		 *//*
		 * probe response frame format
	 	 *	[8] time stamp
		 *	[2] beacon interval
		 *	[2] capability information
		 *	[tlv] ssid
		 *	[tlv] supported rates
		 *	[7] FH/DS parameter set
		 *	[tlv] IBSS parameter set
		 *	[tlv] country code
		 *	[3] power constraint
		 *	[4] tpc report
		 *	[tlv] Channel Switch Announcement
		 *	[3] extended rate phy (ERP)
		 *	[tlv] extended supported rates
		 *	[tlv] WME parameters
		 *	[tlv] WPA/RSN parameters
		 *	[tlv] Atheros Advanced Capabilities
		 *	[tlv] AtherosXR parameters
		 *	[tlv] Quantenna parameters (probe resp)
		 *      [tlv] QTN IE
		 *//* time stamp *//* beacon interval *//* capability information *//* ssid *//* supported rates *//* FH/DS parameters max(7,3) *//* XXX allocate max size *//* IBSS parameter set*//* country code *//* BSS load *//* power constraint *//* tpc report *//*	CSA	*//* ERP *//* XXX !WPA1+WPA2 fits w/o a cluster *//* recoveredRRMIE reserve *//* timestamp should be filled later *//* beacon interval *//* cap. info *//* ssid *//* supported rates *//* XXX: FH/DS parameter set, correct ? *//* TODO: ATIM window *//*
		 * Tight coupling between Country IE and Power Constraint IE
		 * Both using IEEE80211_FEXT_COUNTRYIE to optional enable them.
		 *//* country code *//* power constraint *//* Transmit power envelope *//*TPC Report*//* tx power would be updated in macfw *//* link margin is 0 *//*	CSA	*//* ERP *//* 802.11n specific IEs *//* Ext. Supp. Rates *//* WME *//* WPA *//* AthAdvCaps *//* VHT Operation element *//* QTN 2.4G VHT IE *//* Add Quantenna extender IE *//* QTN WME IE *//*
		 * Deduce whether we're doing open authentication or
		 * shared key authentication.  We do the latter if
		 * we're in the middle of a shared key authentication
		 * handshake or if we're initiating an authentication
		 * request and configured to use shared key.
		 *//* sequence number *//* status *//* XXX not right for shared key *//* Buffer for IWEVENT message *//* Buffer for IWEVENT message *//* reason *//* port closed *//*
		 * asreq frame format
		 *	[2] capability information
		 *	[2] listen interval
		 *	[6*] current AP address (reassoc only)
		 *	[tlv] ssid
		 *	[tlv] supported rates
		 *	[4] power capability (802.11h)
		 *	[54] supported channels element (802.11h)
		 *	[tlv] extended supported rates
		 *	[tlv] WME [if enabled and AP capable]
		 *      [tlv] Atheros advanced capabilities
		 *	[tlv] user-specified ie's
		 *      [tlv] QTN IE
		 *//* IEEE80211_M_STA *//*
		 * NB: Some 11a AP's reject the request when
		 *     short premable is set.
		 *//* Capability information *//* listen interval *//* Current AP address *//* ssid *//* supported rates *//* Ext. Capabilities - For AP mode hostapd adds the extended cap *//* ext. supp. rates *//* power capability/supported channels
		 * in chapter 8.3.3.5, power capability IE is right after extended supported rates
		 * and before supported channels
		 * *//* Supported Channels *//* WME *//* ath adv. cap *//* Setup default key index for static wep case *//* 802.11ac vht capability *//* QTN 2.4G VHT IE *//* User-spec *//* Add QTN Pairing IE *//*
		 * asreq frame format
		 *	[2] capability information
		 *	[2] status
		 *	[2] association ID
		 *	[tlv] supported rates
		 *	[tlv] extended supported rates
		 *      [tlv] WME (if enabled and STA enabled)
		 *      [tlv] Atheros Advanced Capabilities
		 *      [tlv] QTN IE
		 *      [tlv] VSP IE
		 *//* recoveredRRMIE reserve *//* Capability Information *//* status *//* Assoc ID *//* supported rates *//* 802.11w / PMF Timeout element *//* ext. suppo. rates *//* WME *//* athAdvCap *//* QTN WME IE *//* VHT Operation element *//* QTN 2.4G VHT IE *//* Add QTN Pairing IE. *//* reason *//* action header *//* dialog token *//* tpc request ie *//* action header *//* dialog token *//* tpc report ie *//* Form the HT SM PS frame - change of mode for this client. *//* Single byte argument, which is formatted as per 802.11n d11.0 section 7.3.1.22 *//* action header *//* SMPS state change *//* New power save mode *//* action header *//* dialog *//* BA params *//* BA timeout *//* BA sequence control *//* fill ba dialog *//* fill ba params (non half word aligned) *//* fill ba timeout (non half word aligned) *//* fill sequence control (non half word aligned) *//* action header *//* dialog *//* status *//* BA params *//* BA timeout *//* fill ba dialog *//* fill ba status (non half word aligned) *//* fill ba params (non half word aligned) *//* fill ba timeout (non half word aligned) *//* action header *//* DELBA params *//* DELBA reason *//* fill ba params (non half word aligned) *//* fill ba reason (non half word aligned) *//* FIXME: Work out which vendor specific type to output. *//* fall through if condition is not true *//* NOTREACHED *//*
 * Send PS-POLL from to bss. Should only be called when as STA.
 *//*
 * Send DELBA management frame.
