		 *//* Mark the channel as not_available and ready for cac *//* Remove the CSA IE from beacons and cause other field in beacon updated *//* record channel change event *//*
 * Start a CSA process: CSA beacon/action will be sent to STA to notify the CS.
 * @finish_csa: At the CS time, finish_csa() will be called to do the actual CS. If not provided,
 * ieee80211_finish_csa() will be called as default action.
 * @flag: specify whether to use CSA beacon or CSA action or both.
 *//* now flag the beacon update to include the channel switch IE *//* send broadcast csa action *//* Update beacon to include CSA IE *//*
	 * Store original attenuation to handle the following case:
	 * We switched to low power channel when attenuation is small. But then in low
	 * power channel attenuation increases but interference is low. We need to detect
	 * such rate ratio drop to trigger channel ranking.
	 *//* for dfs reentry demon *//*
 * Generate an interference mitigation event
 *//* Choose the channel with maximal power setting *//* All powers are same, run random selection per request *//* There is a potential race condition here, but the timer will kick in and recover it.
	 * Currently we don't plan to protect against it *//*
 * Interference mitigation sampling task
 * Periodically go off-channel to sample the quality of another channel.
 *///FIXME check threshold/* Only sample if at least one VAP is in run state and none are scanning *//* Currently we don't apply the thresholds of FAT and preamble error to QHop case *//* For STA mode, always send cca report to AP *//* Don't switch channel under basic WDS mode *//* But channel switch is now possible on the WDS link if it is an MBS *//* set to -1 helps to discard first report after assoc or channel switch *//*
 * Clean SCS state with different clean levels.
